  "details": "In the depth pass of imposter generation, the default \"Hidden\" shader is still visible, which causes the depth to be wrong in the parallax shader. This makes things like glasses with totally invisible lenses, or accessories that are meant to be turned off, look weird and have a depth effect anyway on the imposter.",
